-- title:
--   Frobenius twists satisfy the weight-k Hecke congruence mod p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N$ a natural number, and $f$ a cusp form of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ which is a normalised eigenform in the sense of the project predicate `IsNormalizedEigenform`: writing $a_n(f)$ for the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $f$ (at width $1$), one has $a_1(f)=1$, $a_{mn}(f)=a_m(f)a_n(f)$ whenever $m$ and $n$ are coprime, $a_{q^{r+2}}(f)=a_q(f)a_{q^{r+1}}(f)-q\,a_{q^r}(f)$ for every prime $q\nmid N$ and every $r$, and $a_{q^{r+2}}(f)=a_q(f)a_{q^{r+1}}(f)$ for every prime $q\mid N$. Let $a:\mathbb{N}\to\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$, where $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ denotes the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$, be a system of lifts, so that the image of $a_n$ in $\mathbb{C}$ equals $a_n(f)$ for all $n$. Let $j,k$ be natural numbers with $2\le k$ and $(p-1)\mid(k-2)$ (natural subtraction), let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid N$, and let $n$ be a natural number. Then, for the formal weight-$k$ Hecke operator $T_\ell=U_\ell+\ell^{k-1}V_\ell$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}\llbracket X\rrbracket$, which sends a series with coefficients $c_m$ to the series whose $n$-th coefficient is $c_{\ell n}+\ell^{k-1}c_{n/\ell}$ when $\ell\mid n$ and $c_{\ell n}$ otherwise, the element
--   $$\mathrm{coeff}_n\bigl(T_\ell\bigl(\textstyle\sum_m a_m^{p^j}X^m\bigr)\bigr)-a_\ell^{p^j}a_n^{p^j}$$
--   lies in the ideal of $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ generated by $p$.
--
--   This is the statement that the $p^j$-th Frobenius twist of the coefficient system of a weight-$2$ normalised eigenform is, modulo $p$, a formal eigenvector of the weight-$k$ Hecke operator $T_\ell$ at every good prime $\ell$, for any weight $k\equiv 2 \pmod{p-1}$ — the congruence between Hecke actions in weights congruent modulo $p-1$. It is used in the construction of an ideal of the Hecke algebra attached to a newform whose level is divisible by a square, via [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_ordCompl_of_isNewform_sq_dvd`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_ordCompl_of_isNewform_sq_dvd).
